From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 13:10:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 43/62] verimark: set enroll-date + IT-aware description on
 enroll success

Two bugs were tripping the fprintd crash visible during delete
and post-verify on the IT path :

1. The enroll-date was never explicitly set. fprintd's
   delete_enrolled_fingers and verify_cb log the print metadata
   via g_log %s, which calls strlen on NULL and SEGVs. The
   verimark_print_from_tuid fallback path already had a comment
   warning about this and set a synthetic GDate ; the primary
   enroll-success path forgot it.

2. The description was hardcoded as 'Kensington VeriMark DT'
   even when the device is the IT. Cosmetic but fix it while
   we're here, PID-aware now.

Set both defensively if NULL (= fprintd didn't supply them) :
- description : DT / IT label based on g_usb_device_get_pid
- enroll-date : today's GDate (only used as display hint by
                fprintd, not part of identity matching)

Resolves the 'fprintd dumped core in delete_enrolled_fingers' and
'fprintd dumped core in verify_cb -> check_local_storage' SEGVs
observed during IT runtime tests.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index d3bc8d1..ce2c9dd 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -2688,10 +2688,26 @@ enroll_sm_done(FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev, GError *error)
         fpi_print_set_type(template, FPI_PRINT_RAW);
         fpi_print_set_device_stored(template, TRUE);
         g_object_set(template, "fpi-data", data, NULL);
+        /* PID-aware description (DT vs IT). */
+        GUsbDevice *usb = fpi_device_get_usb_device(dev);
+        const gboolean is_it = (usb != NULL &&
+                                g_usb_device_get_pid(usb) == VERIMARK_PID_IT);
         if (fp_print_get_description(template) == NULL)
-            fp_print_set_description(template, "Kensington VeriMark DT");
+            fp_print_set_description(template,
+                is_it ? "Kensington VeriMark IT"
+                       : "Kensington VeriMark DT");
         if (fp_print_get_username(template) == NULL)
             fp_print_set_username(template, "verimark");
+        /* fprintd logs print metadata during cleanup and crashes if
+         * enroll-date is NULL — same g_log %s on NULL → strlen fault
+         * the fallback path warns about below. Set a synthetic stamp
+         * if fprintd didn't (the value is only used as display hint). */
+        if (fp_print_get_enroll_date(template) == NULL) {
+            GDate *today = g_date_new();
+            g_date_set_time_t(today, time(NULL));
+            fp_print_set_enroll_date(template, today);
+            g_date_free(today);
+        }
         fpi_device_enroll_complete(dev, g_object_ref(template), NULL);
     } else {
         /* Defensive fallback (shouldn't trigger on a real enroll). */
